    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To determine the total number of games played in a baseball league with nine teams, where each team plays three games with each of the other teams exactly once, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the number of unique pairs of teams:**\n   The number of ways to choose 2 teams out of 9 is given by the combination formula \\( \\binom{n}{k} \\), which represents the number of ways to choose \\( k \\) elements from a set of \\( n \\) elements without regard to the order of selection. Here, \\( n = 9 \\) and \\( k = 2 \\):\n   \\[\n   \\binom{9}{2} = \\frac{9!}{2!(9-2)!} = \\frac{9!}{2! \\cdot 7!} = \\frac{9 \\times 8 \\times 7!}{2 \\times 1 \\times 7!} = \\frac{9 \\times 8}{2 \\times 1} = 36\n   \\]\n   So, there are 36 unique pairs of teams.\n\n2. **Determine the number of games each pair plays:**\n   Each pair of teams plays 3 games with each other team. Therefore, each pair of teams will play 3 games with each of the other 7 teams. This means each pair of teams plays:\n   \\[\n   3 \\times 7 = 21 \\text{ games}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the total number of games:**\n   Since there are 36 pairs of teams and each pair plays 21 games, the total number of games played is:\n   \\[\n   36 \\times 21 = 756\n   \\]\n\nThus, the total number of games played in the league is \\(\\boxed{756}\\).",
