    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "The total number of games played depends on the number of teams in the league and the number of games played between any two teams. \n\nThe number of ways to choose two teams from nine without regard to order (since the order in which we play the games doesn’t matter) is given by the combination formula:\n\n$\\binom{n}{k} = \\frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!}$\n\nwhere n is the total number of teams and k is the number of teams chosen at a time. In this case, we want to choose 2 teams out of 9, so:\n\n$\\binom{9}{2} = \\frac{9!}{2!(9-2)!} = \\frac{9 \\times 8}{2 \\times 1} = 36$\n\nThis means there are 36 unique pairs of teams. Since each pair plays exactly three games, the total number of games is:\n\n$36 \\times 3 = 108$\n\nSo, the total number of games played during the season is $\\boxed{108}$.",
