    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To determine the total number of games played in the baseball league, we need to calculate the number of unique matchups between the teams and then multiply by the number of games each matchup involves.\n\nFirst, let's identify the number of unique matchups between the teams. Since there are 9 teams, the number of ways to choose 2 teams out of 9 is given by the combination formula \\( \\binom{n}{k} \\), which represents the number of ways to choose \\( k \\) elements from a set of \\( n \\) elements without regard to the order of selection. Here, \\( n = 9 \\) and \\( k = 2 \\):\n\n\\[\n\\binom{9}{2} = \\frac{9!}{2!(9-2)!} = \\frac{9!}{2! \\cdot 7!} = \\frac{9 \\times 8 \\times 7!}{2 \\times 1 \\times 7!} = \\frac{9 \\times 8}{2 \\times 1} = 36\n\\]\n\nSo, there are 36 unique matchups between the teams.\n\nNext, each matchup involves 3 games. Therefore, the total number of games played is the number of unique matchups multiplied by the number of games per matchup:\n\n\\[\n36 \\times 3 = 108\n\\]\n\nThus, the total number of games played in the season is \\(\\boxed{108}\\).",
